  "ingredients": [
    "2 tablespoons olive oil",
    "3 tablespoons all-purpose flour",
    "2 pounds beef chuck, cut into 1 1/2-inch cubes",
    "1 pound carrots, peeled and cut into 1-inch chunks",
    "6 large potatoes, peeled and cut into large chunks",
    "1 white onion, cut into large chunks",
    "2 cloves garlic, minced",
    "2 cups beef broth",
    "1 (6 ounce) can tomato paste",
    "1 (12 fluid ounce) can or bottle Irish stout beer (e.g. Guinness(r))",
    "1 tablespoon cold water",
    "1 tablespoon cornstarch"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather the ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/jE46lEEaRAEGrT_iQFbc0Bo4wfM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/100839-irish-beef-stew-DDMFS-006-step-01-3fe3745288d243d98fc5bebd6a0e6786.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/100839/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat oil in a large skillet over medium heat. Toss beef cubes with flour to coat, then fry in the hot oil until browned.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/YfRgm3h1nu6wQS224xmS2qMIVFQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/100839-irish-beef-stew-DDMFS-010-step-02-edcbd4f02e98430ea16532620840f0ba.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/100839/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place carrots, potatoes, onion, and garlic into a large slow cooker; place browned beef on top of vegetables. Mix beef broth and tomato paste together until combined; pour into the slow cooker along with beer.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/hr6mWIbvxB3A5hSXGtMuCL4Spa0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/100839-irish-beef-stew-DDMFS-012-step-03-de54351e08484c89ba37d6c88c27f89a.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/100839/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cover and cook on High for 6 hours or Low for 8 hours. During the last hour before serving, dissolve cornstarch in cold water and stir into broth. Simmer on the High setting for a few minutes to thicken. Serve hot.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
